# 26. FINANCIAL ACCOUNTING RULES

Shared Udhar must remain separate from normal Income and Expense accounting.

## Borrowed money

Loan Received / Udhar Taken is not earned income.

## Money lent

Udhar Given is not an ordinary expense.

## Repayment received

A repayment received should reduce receivable balance and must not automatically be treated as new income.

## Repayment paid

A repayment paid should reduce payable balance and must not automatically be counted as a normal expense again.

Avoid double-counting money in:

- Income
- Expenses
- Net worth
- Cash flow
- Financial Flow
- Available balance
- Reports
- Charts

Integrate the Udhar system with the main dashboard only where financially logic supports it.

